{
 "name": "hatchback_car",
 "notes": "Concept layout of a small front-wheel-drive hatchback (automobile, car, saloon, sedan), built from separate parts so it can be pulled apart, weighed and drawn. Front is +X, wheels on the ground at z = 0. Body: floor, side panels with wheel arches and door openings, end panels, hood, deck, roof, windscreen, rear window, side glasses, two doors, all sheet metal `wall` thick. Interior: seats and a fuel tank. Powertrain: an inline four engine and, ahead of it, a gearbox with two gear pairs on parallel shafts, keyways and backlash. Exhaust: pipe, muffler, tail pipe. Driveline: the countershaft runs back to a differential housing on the front axle, with a half shaft to each wheel. Not modelled: the crown wheel, pinion and CV joints, suspension, steering, pedals, lights, wiring. Not crash-rated or road-legal.",
